# Hides snapd's start-up check image from udisks2. At every start snapd checks that the kernel
# can mount squashfs: it mounts a 4 KiB image from /tmp/syscheck-squashfs-* through a loop device
# and unmounts it at once (snapd's syscheck/squashfs.go). The session's udiskie --automount keeps
# every loop device with a backing file (its default filters skip only /var/lib/snapd/snaps/*),
# so it tried to mount the image too: a loop device is not removable, udisks2 asked polkit for
# org.freedesktop.udisks2.filesystem-mount-system, and the session showed an administrator
# password dialog whenever snapd started (the distro's boot test, 2026-10-19). With
# UDISKS_IGNORE set, udisks2 marks the device as hidden, and neither udiskie nor Files acts on it.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="loop[0-9]*", ACTION=="add|change", ATTR{loop/backing_file}=="/tmp/syscheck-squashfs-*", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
